    # r100 --fixed-fps scheduler lattice: r100_fpslat.gd drives byte-identical
    # copies of the r100 boundary probes (corpus/fixtures/r100_probe_r100b_*.gd,
    # recopied into each child as res://r100b_*.gd) as bounded children
    # (timeout -s KILL, engine flags before --script, script args after --)
    # in fresh per-cell projects across GodotPhysics, Jolt, and Dummy. Each
    # cell's normalized stream (banner/time/Object-ids masked, Jolt job-system
    # warning allowlisted) pins a sha256-16; the whole aggregate line is the
    # receipt. Every signature below was live-derived on the final bytes; no
    # pin was authored from scout/boundary text. Expected-error classes stay
    # in the hash and are counted (ee=): arerr is the deterministic
    # body_shape_entered RID->Object callback diagnostic (once per non-dummy
    # receipt), wm is the --write-movie headless crash head (stream truncated
    # at the deterministic 'at:' line before the ASLR backtrace; rc=134 =
    # SIGABRT after the signal-11 handler), lerr/lfin are the lifecycle
    # script-error classes, leak the ObjectDB class. beq=1 asserts
    # backend-equal normalized streams (Dummy only diverges where the server
    # genuinely differs: ray=miss, e_first=-1, or the non-integrating traj
    # hash). inert=1 cells pin the equals-form/--suffix flag traps; eq=N cells
    # assert a sha match with the named baseline cell. unbound cells assert
    # rc=137 via the outer timeout while still booting (boot=1,tickge1=1).
    # Sized for the 20 s case cap: quit0 proves '--quit-after 0 disables the
    # bound' at 4000 backend-equal ticks.
